00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:14.680
And this is all described
in the User Guide here.

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:19.300
So you can see how you can
add the image that you're

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:24.070
looking for specifically, if
you are generating a manifest.

00:07:24.070 --> 00:07:28.060
But you can also use the
deployApp, deployAPI,

00:07:28.060 --> 00:07:31.300
deployDoc, deploySite
functions from RS Connect.

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:36.570
And similar functions exist
for RS Connect Python as well.

00:07:36.570 --> 00:07:41.250
If there isn't an image that
matches the version of R

00:07:41.250 --> 00:07:44.370
or Python that you need,
you'll get the same type

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:46.470
of deployment error
as you would today

00:07:46.470 --> 00:07:52.170
using local execution
with local processes

00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:55.680
if there isn't a version of
R or Python on your server

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:58.100
that's available.

00:07:58.100 --> 00:07:58.690
All right.

00:07:58.690 --> 00:08:02.320
So hopefully, that
has reasonably

00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:06.550
convinced you that the
user experience isn't

00:08:06.550 --> 00:08:10.780
going to change remarkably,
although you can now target

00:08:10.780 --> 00:08:13.390
