00:14:46.080 --> 00:14:48.290
New File.

00:14:48.290 --> 00:14:51.500
And this first part is
going to set the replicas,

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:54.840
and then I'm going to
configure shared storage here.

00:14:54.840 --> 00:14:57.026
So I'm going to grab all that.

00:14:57.026 --> 00:15:00.830
So back in, Connect
needs shared storage.

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:02.630
Needs to be mounted in.

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:06.920
You need to create a Persistent
Volume Claim and give it a name

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:07.730
here.

00:15:07.730 --> 00:15:12.190
And this name is arbitrary
that's used in a couple places

00:15:12.190 --> 00:15:12.690
here.

00:15:12.690 --> 00:15:15.050
So make sure if you
change that, that you

00:15:15.050 --> 00:15:17.930
change it all the places
that it needs to be changed.

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:23.070
You're going to create
a storage class for NFS,

00:15:23.070 --> 00:15:25.450
tell it how much storage
you're requesting.

00:15:25.450 --> 00:15:28.720
And then finally,
enable the launcher.

00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:32.780
And that's all there is to it.

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:41.870
So if I Save out here and
name it values.yaml, Save.

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:42.850
All right.

00:15:42.850 --> 00:15:45.090
Now I am good to go.

00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:49.470
And from here, your
process for using Helm

00:15:49.470 --> 00:15:52.890
is to change this
values.yaml file

00:15:52.890 --> 00:15:58.260
and then run this command
here, helm template, the chart

00:15:58.260 --> 00:16:00.450
with your values.yaml.

00:16:00.450 --> 00:16:04.350
And this sort of pattern,
updating your values.yaml

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:07.470
and then checking
it on helm template,

00:16:07.470 --> 00:16:11.670
will show you how your values
file affects the template.

00:16:11.670 --> 00:16:18.870
And that's what my buddy Cole
and Helm wizard calls the bread

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:20.700
and butter of using Helm.

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:21.840
This is the power.

00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:25.620
And it's also going to be
really useful as we interact

00:16:25.620 --> 00:16:30.450
with you because you can send
us your values.yaml file,

00:16:30.450 --> 00:16:33.960
and then we at RStudio
on the Support side

00:16:33.960 --> 00:16:37.500
can run this same
helm template command

00:16:37.500 --> 00:16:39.735
and see exactly
what you're saying.

00:16:39.735 --> 00:16:43.830
We can see how your
values.yaml file is going

00:16:43.830 --> 00:16:48.080
to interact with the template.

00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:50.493
So that's really useful.

00:16:50.493 --> 00:16:51.910
The other section
that we're going

00:16:51.910 --> 00:16:54.730
to want to add to
this values.yaml file

00:16:54.730 --> 00:16:58.010
is some configuration
for Connect itself.

00:16:58.010 --> 00:17:01.960
So this is where the things
that you would traditionally

00:17:01.960 --> 00:17:04.359
put in your go
configuration file

00:17:04.359 --> 00:17:06.680
are going to get dumped instead.

00:17:06.680 --> 00:17:10.390
So let's add that.

00:17:10.390 --> 00:17:15.849
And you'll see that we
are adding a database

00:17:15.849 --> 00:17:16.750
configuration.

00:17:16.750 --> 00:17:18.400
We're saying it's
going to be Postgres,

00:17:18.400 --> 00:17:22.839
and that will overwrite
the default of SQLite.

00:17:22.839 --> 00:17:24.550
And then give it an address.

00:17:24.550 --> 00:17:28.480
Again, if you're using
the Connect namespace,

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:33.280
the RStudio-Connect namespace,
that URL should be correct.

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:38.470
And then you're just
going to provide

00:17:38.470 --> 00:17:41.530
the same persistent
volume claim name

00:17:41.530 --> 00:17:43.690
for this new section
of configuration

00:17:43.690 --> 00:17:45.460
for Connect Launcher.

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:49.120
And that should match
what you had up here.

00:17:49.120 --> 00:17:50.770
So let's save that out.

00:17:50.770 --> 00:17:54.220
And now if I did
everything correct,

00:17:54.220 --> 00:17:57.400
we should be able to
helm install Connect.

00:17:57.400 --> 00:17:58.315
Let's give it a shot.

00:18:01.450 --> 00:18:05.550
Installing it now.

00:18:05.550 --> 00:18:07.017
Get pods.

